  "notes": "Both verses address the Prophet ﷺ; no plate on his self-description («وما أنا عليكم بوكيل»): the two paths leave before it. As-Sa'di's «ولا يضر الله شيئًا» (3:144 wording) and his closing «بالسيف والسنان» are not used. Light for «قد جاءكم الحق», two paths for «فمن اهتدى… ومن ضل», geometric for «حتى يحكم الله». STAGING v4: c1 (108): O mankind (the Prophet ﷺ is told to say it): the people addressed, a mixed group of five faceless people in a town by day, held wide or in close-up; the camera only: nobody speaks, points or turns toward an empty side, no plate starts on 108:1, and nothing of whoever is guided / whoever strays (a general conditional) is acted. A light plate for the truth has come to you (108:5-8) and a two-paths plate for guidance and straying (108:9-18), gone before his self-description (108:19-22), which is held wide with no pan. c2 (109) stays ambient (dawn, no threat): the command to the Prophet ﷺ himself to follow the revelation and be patient (his own conduct is never staged); params.quiet over 109:1-8; a geometric plate for until Allah judges (109:7-11). Cover on c2 (holding to the revelation)."
